questions.explanationText:
$$A = \left[ {\matrix{
0 & 0 & { - 1} \cr
0 & { - 1} & 0 \cr
{ - 1} & 0 & 0 \cr

} } \right]$$

clearly $$\,\,\,A \ne 0.\,$$ Also $$\,\,\left| A \right| = - 1 \ne 0$$

$$\therefore$$ $${A^{ - 1}}\,\,$$ exists, further

$$\left( { - 1} \right)I = \left[ {\matrix{
{ - 1} & 0 & 0 \cr
0 & { - 1} & 0 \cr
0 & 0 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right] \ne A$$

Also $${A^2} = \left[ {\matrix{
0 & 0 & { - 1} \cr
0 & { - 1} & 0 \cr
{ - 1} & 0 & 0 \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
0 & 0 & { - 1} \cr
0 & { - 1} & 0 \cr
{ - 1} & 0 & 0 \cr

} } \right]$$

$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
1 & 0 & 0 \cr
0 & 1 & 0 \cr
0 & 0 & 1 \cr

} } \right] = I$$

